  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\nHighs today are expected to be within a few degrees of yesterday. \nWeak ridging aloft and weak offshore flow will continue to keep \nhighs above average. Along the coast, daytime highs are expected to \nrun 10 to 15 degrees above average through Wednesday, with highs 5 \nto 10 degrees above average elsewhere. Thursday, highs will be up to \n5 degrees cooler than Wednesday but will still be 5 to 10 degrees \nabove average. \n\nThursday, an upper level low will dig south and east and is expected \nto pass through Northern Baja by early Friday. This will bring \nperiods of mostly light showers to the coastal basin Friday into \nSaturday. There will be a modest increase in precipitable water, \nwith some guidance showing a bump up in IVT on Friday. The ECMWF EPS \nhas a 30% chance of IVT exceeding 250 kg/m/s (equates to a weak \natmospheric river), while the GEFS has closer to a 60% chance. There \nis still quite a bit of spread in rainfall amounts, especially for \nareas north of San Diego County with some members still running \ncompletely dry. Solutions that usher more IVT into Southern \nCalifornia will lead to higher rainfall amounts across the area. \nCompared to yesterday, the upper end of potential rainfall totals \nhas come down to under an inch. The NBM chances of exceeding 0.50\" \nover 48 hours from Friday morning to early Sunday is 15-35% \nacross the coastal basin. \n\nPeriods of showers are expected through the weekend into early next \nweek as troughs line up to periodically pass across the US West \nCoast. A lot of the details will become clearer as the timing and \ntrack of each trough passage becomes clearer. After the \nFriday/Saturday timeframe, there may be periods of isolated light \nshowers Sunday, but ensemble guidance is honing in on Monday/Tuesday \nfor our next chance at widespread rainfall. \n\nWinds are expected to increase over the mountains and deserts with \neach trough passage. Expect winds to increase as early as late \nThursday and continue into Saturday morning. Peak gusts of 35 to\n45 mph, with gusts up to 55 mph through wind prone passes. Winds \nare expected to increase again early next week with the next \ntrough passage.",
